Two **Svelte 5** components: `App.svelte` keeps the count with `$state`, and `GelButton.svelte` takes a `label` and an `onclick` with `$props`. Press **Start** in the preview and it is compiled right in your browser!

~~~ file: App.svelte
<script>
    import GelButton from './GelButton.svelte';
    let count = $state(0);
    let double = $derived(count * 2);
</script>

<main>
    <h1>Gel counter</h1>
    <p>You pressed it <b>{count}</b> time{count === 1 ? '' : 's'} (double is {double})!</p>
    <GelButton label="Press me!" onclick={() => count++} />
    <GelButton label="Reset" green onclick={() => (count = 0)} />
</main>

<style>
    main { font-family: "Segoe UI", system-ui, sans-serif; color: #10324d; }
    h1 { color: #0a5c99; }
</style>
~~~

~~~ file: GelButton.svelte
<script>
    let { label = 'Button', green = false, onclick } = $props();
</script>

<button class:green {onclick}>{label}</button>

<style>
    button {
        margin-right: 8px;
        padding: 9px 22px;
        border: 1px solid rgba(0, 60, 120, 0.45);
        border-radius: 999px;
        color: #fff;
        font: 700 16px system-ui, sans-serif;
        text-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 40, 90, 0.5);
        background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55) 0%, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05) 50%, transparent 51%), linear-gradient(180deg, #7fd3ff, #0a74c9);
        box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8), 0 3px 8px rgba(10, 116, 201, 0.3);
        cursor: pointer;
    }
    .green { background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55) 0%, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05) 50%, transparent 51%), linear-gradient(180deg, #b6f08a, #2e9a1c); }
</style>
~~~
